I brought it inside. Set it on the table. Stood in my chamber and breathed.

The left breast throbbed. The right ached in sympathy. The welt from the bowstring was hot beneath the corset   a thin line of fire across a curve that should not have been there but was, undeniably, irrevocably //was//.

I began to unlace the training leathers. The chest piece came free, the leather stiff with dried sweat. The corset beneath was damp, the grey linen darkened to charcoal across the chest and under the arms. I reached behind me and fumbled with the lacing   my fingers were more dextrous than they had been, longer and thinner, but the angle was awkward and the leather had tightened with sweat.

