Beneath the corset, the damage was evident.

The left breast bore a thin, angry welt across its outer curve   a scarlet line perhaps four inches long, drawn diagonally from the upper edge of the breast toward the inframammary fold. The bowstring's path, recorded in flesh. The skin surrounding the welt was flushed, hot to the touch, and the tissue beneath was visibly swollen   the breast appearing slightly larger than its partner, not from growth but from inflammation.

